86282128 1111 #uuid "f77af5f4-17af-5bd0-b2f6-b4c21847c184" 13194139534205 true] [17592186282129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282130 13194139534205 true] [17592186282129 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534205 true] [17592186282129 1041 "field-2" 13194139534205 true] [17592186282129 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282130 13194139534205 true] [17592186282129 1110 #uuid "2551328a-5b05-501e-96e8-16b3a07747e7" 13194139534205 true] [17592186282130 1034 "7" 13194139534205 true] [17592186282130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534205 true] [17592186282130 1111 #uuid "0fd3f57e-7d66-5461-8dbd-6397eb3639c7" 13194139534205 true] [17592186282131 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282132 13194139534205 true] [17592186282131 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282134 13194139534205 true] [17592186282131 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282136 13194139534205 true] [17592186282131 1089 "q-276744" 13194139534205 true] [17592186282131 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534205 true] [17592186282131 1100 "Solve the inequality $-\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{4+5x}+6\\ge 2.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\le $\n{{field-3}}" 13194139534205 true] [17592186282131 1113 #uuid "223ae82c-5013-5c43-be8d-095a6256031a" 13194139534205 true] [17592186282131 1145 "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{4+5x}+6 & \\ge 2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{4+5x} & \\ge -4 \\\\ \\sqrt{4+5x} & \\le 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the sign of the inequality since we divided by a negative number\n\nIn this inequality, the square root is being compared to a non-negative number $(12).$ So, we can square both sides of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt{4+5x})}^{2} & \\le {12}^{2} \\\\ 4+5x & \\le 144 \\\\ 5x & \\le 140 \\\\ x & \\le 28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must only keep the solutions that are in the domain of the square root. To find the domain of the square root, we recall that the argument of the square root must be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4+5x & \\ge 0 \\\\ 5x & \\ge